From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:04:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gicv3): let a platform read a core's Redistributor base

The driver records where each core's Redistributor frame is, in the
rdistif_base_addrs[] array the platform hands it (or, with
USE_GIC_DRIVER=3, the one in gicv3_base.c), from the walk over
GICR_TYPER in gicv3_driver_init() or the core's own
gicv3_rdistif_probe(). Platform code that has to touch a Redistributor
register the driver does not manage, such as an IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED
power sequence around a cluster power-down, has no way to get at that
address and ends up computing it from a fixed stride of its own: a
second source for the same address, which disagrees with the driver as
soon as the frames are not in core order or are larger (GICv4 VLPI
frames).

Add gicv3_rdistif_get_base(proc_num), which returns the recorded base
address, or 0 while the core's frame has not been found.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 include/drivers/arm/gicv3.h     |  1 +
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c b/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
index 7ef5559f2..fde273175 100644
--- a/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
+++ b/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
@@ -1419,6 +1419,20 @@ int gicv3_rdistif_probe(const uintptr_t gicr_frame)
 	return 0; /* Found matching GICR frame */
 }
 
+/*******************************************************************************
+ * This function returns the base address of the Redistributor frame of the
+ * core 'proc_num', as found by gicv3_driver_init() or by that core's
+ * gicv3_rdistif_probe(). It returns 0 while the frame has not been found.
+ ******************************************************************************/
+uintptr_t gicv3_rdistif_get_base(unsigned int proc_num)
+{
+	assert(gicv3_driver_data != NULL);
+	assert(gicv3_driver_data->rdistif_base_addrs != NULL);
+	assert(proc_num < gicv3_driver_data->rdistif_num);
+
+	return gicv3_driver_data->rdistif_base_addrs[proc_num];
+}
+
 /******************************************************************************
  * This function checks the interrupt ID and returns true for SGIs, (E)PPIs
  * and (E)SPIs IDs. Any interrupt ID outside the range is invalid and returns
diff --git a/include/drivers/arm/gicv3.h b/include/drivers/arm/gicv3.h
index 8669f97f4..a88f8eb5d 100644
--- a/include/drivers/arm/gicv3.h
+++ b/include/drivers/arm/gicv3.h
@@ -543,6 +543,7 @@ typedef struct gicv3_its_ctx {
 void gicv3_driver_init(const gicv3_driver_data_t *plat_driver_data);
 void gicv3_driver_init_default(void);
 int gicv3_rdistif_probe(const uintptr_t gicr_frame);
+uintptr_t gicv3_rdistif_get_base(unsigned int proc_num);
 void gicv3_distif_init(void);
 void gicv3_rdistif_init(unsigned int proc_num);
 void gicv3_rdistif_on(unsigned int proc_num);
